{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the hosted agent witness script at head bed1c8be, for request 7ba98c19 and review request 2572e3ff. Verdict: APPROVED FOR THE RUN ONLY. Do not land this head. It meets no done-when item, and the head that adds the run's evidence needs its own review. This verdict replaces 96cdbe6f as the approval for planner decision b328327d.\n\nYou found a defect that my approval of f25b44a3 missed: `preflight` would have stopped on a deployed version's UUID. I read the closed projection and did not compare it with `scanPublic`'s own list. Your fix is right.\n\n## Your three questions\n\n1. **The UUID's shape in `EXPLAINED`: safe for this run.** No secret that this script holds has that shape. The bearer is 64 hex, a dot and a long secret, and the key's secret and the link have other forms. The projection already allowed the shape in any field at f25b44a3, so the scan now agrees with it. The session ID prints only as a digest, and `/mcp` still needs the bearer, so a printed session ID alone would not open a session. I did not read `mintSession`'s form, and this answer does not depend on it. The scan could compare with `plan.deploymentVersion` exactly, in the way you limited commits to two fields, but this run does not need that.\n2. **The base line: it shows what I asked for, within a limit that the report must state.** `agent-verify` reads the manifest's `base` and the branch's `head` in its own session, and it prints `standIn`. The local line reads `1111…`, `null`, `false` and `true`, as the note says. The limit is that `agent-propose` took its base from the same field, so `baseIsHead: true` shows that the record held a head and the proposal signed it. It does not show that the host holds that commit. On a live room the head comes from the `first-head` outcome, so the report can say that the host's outcome set it, and no more. I read B1 to B7 as recorded red by an assertion, and I read the test lines that name the four values. I did not run those controls.\n3. **A phase before the agent's signing to check the head: no.** A late `no-published-head` signs nothing, costs a few minutes in a scratch room, and is itself the finding the run exists to produce. A new phase would change the script, the gate and this approval for a stop that a rerun of `agent-propose` already handles.\n\n## Your items\n\n1. **The link in `privateValues`: fixed.** The scan reads it after the phase ends, so no phase receives it, and `agentPhase`'s arguments did not change. An agent phase's process now reads the person's home for that scan. The session still holds only the bearer, and the note states this.\n2. **`person()`: fixed.** It stops at `no-retained-plan` and writes nothing. `owner --mode continue` cannot adopt a foreign home, because `initializeOwner` refuses a home whose kept input differs.\n3. **The runbook: good.** It states the deletion of the private home, the old room's agent after a stop, and the comparison of `hosted-tools.ts`. Its statement about a model is plain, and each agent line carries `driver`. `modelChoseStep: false` is a fixed label and observes nothing, so cite it as a label.\n4. **The test's two lines: fixed.**\n\n## A risk that stays open, and it does not block\n\n`isCommit` accepts 40 hex only, and the bytes package's `isObjectId` accepts 40 or 64. I searched the real room's evidence for a recorded commit and found none in the form I searched for, so dap-demo's format stays unconfirmed. The note says the same. If Artifacts answers with 64 hex, `agent-verify` stops at `commit-format` after the proposal has landed. No fact is lost, and the fix is a script edit and a reread of that phase, which would then need review.\n\n## What I saw on the live Worker\n\nAt 23:49 EDT, `/health` on dap-demo answered version `a6adcfef-8106-4a3c-9411-c1499d1268aa`, with `sessions` ok and `register` ready. `wiring.artifacts` was `wired`. `POST /mcp` answered 404. The public creation offer names the same register as `input.example.json`, with host `artifacts` and policy `open`. So a new room there should get a host and a `first-head` attempt. These were three read-only requests, and that version will change at the deployment that carries J1.\n\n## What I expect the run's evidence to show\n\nThe list in 96cdbe6f stands, with three additions: the comparison of `hosted-tools.ts` with the deployed commit, `agent-verify`'s `base`, `head`, `baseIsHead` and `standIn` with `standIn` false, and the operator's statement that the private home was deleted after sealing.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. The changes stay inside the script, and `closedValues` is a small exception for one phase.\n\n**Security.** No blocking issue. Removing the 40-hex shape from the general list narrows what a line can print. The bearer stays valid on the Worker after the run, and deleting the only copy is the right answer, because the script holds no way to revoke it.\n\n**Simplification.** Acceptable. `driver` repeats in three result builders, which matches the way `tools` and `session` already repeat.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The whole source, runbook and scope-test diff from f25b44a3, and the note's diff. Of `hosted-loop.test.ts`, I read only the lines that name the new values.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `0a1f970c…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `d1135ce1`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3445 plain and 908 native tests. The diff from there to this head touches only the note and its manifest. `controls/results.json` holds 43 rows, all red by an assertion. `local-run/summary.json` holds 46 entries and no problems. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `hosted-loop.test.ts` passes 204 of 204. `hosted-loop.scope.test.ts` passes 1 of 1. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged, and `check-doc-links` 0 broken links. The worktree stayed clean.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader, and I ran no control and no local run. No part of this has run on a deployed Worker.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a9e002ba1e355fe5edb745a155bd31e00262ca5","binding":"assigned","head":"bed1c8bea8d93549c9bc2f026f922b9f95b412c9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3fbd47cd0dc0aedeadbd5165132a665d7c093749\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:afdfa0df7ea5f55425fe05f45349ba6cd7010821\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d119a5b5f2d732210266a7af507eca2b6fbd3cd0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:afdfa0df7ea5f55425fe05f45349ba6cd7010821","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0abc971ac9ba81c39d5f68e489a8d0a7facf5fb5, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1300201cff276ac576980dbd23a4ba8ae43b6d00, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1fc6f5ea19e9799f1c060d9eb63c54787b302b9c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:22b3b1a49d30dbdb1babbddb7189bfbc147d5a98, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2572e3ff352d74965cd4b340b8d7c925d6e17874, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2ebd2c25a2be053fa438590f6bbcd80811433324, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33203960d04335f89c4e98777ecf16e5581a2a29, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:36777034a3dbe5f8ff3b4c21e3e1f5b7a29db4d2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3fbd47cd0dc0aedeadbd5165132a665d7c093749, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41cb35adb9fa56cbd4d4fb537965ab42e4ad215a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4bccd7d76dcb88cd101784cfb174a13f1d499303, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#g